  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Quiet Workbench",
    "overview": "OpenQuote is a calm, neutral workspace: an off-white page, zinc greys, hairlines and dashed row rules, cards outlined by a 1px ring with a barely-there layered shadow, and near-black actions. Nothing decorates. The total, the price of each line, where each price came from, and the next action are the only things allowed to speak. One hi-vis orange accent, the colour of site safety gear, appears only when a job is being priced, is still in flight, or needs checking; everything else stays grey so that orange always means \"this is live, look here\".\n\nDensity is a compact desktop workspace from 640px (28 to 36px controls, 12 to 14px labels, 28px nav items, open tables) and stacked and thumb-sized on a phone (44px targets, bottom tab bar, full-screen sheets). Two faces split the work: Figtree at medium weight for headings (page titles, greeting lines, sheet titles), Geist for everything a user operates or reads in a row, with tabular figures wherever money or quantity appears. A dark zinc theme follows the system setting for evening admin. The system refuses both a costume (no trade metaphors drawn into the UI) and the generic SaaS starter (no heavy display type, no icon tiles, no colour on every status).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Neutral zinc ramp on an off-white page carries all structure; primary buttons are a short near-black gradient with a top highlight.",
      "One orange accent, reserved: \"Price this job\", live progress, in-flight status dots, warnings.",
      "Green and red only for confirmation and error.",
      "8px controls, 10px cards, 14px raised cards, 16px wrappers; 1px rings and hairlines; dashed rules between rows.",
      "Figtree 500 for headings, Geist 400/500 for UI, 600 for totals; tabular figures, cents set back in grey.",
      "Status is a grey pill with a word; only in-flight and failed work add a dot.",
      "Open tables: a grey 40px header over a hairline, no frame.",
      "Dotted grid for empty states and the sign-in field."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Orange Rule",
        "body": "Orange marks only the pricing moment, live or in-flight state, and warnings. Orange anywhere else is wrong. At most one accent button per screen.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Grey Status Rule",
        "body": "Status is a grey pill holding a word. Only in-flight work (orange dot) and failed work (red dot) add a dot. Never a rainbow of statuses.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Decoration-Only Rule",
        "body": "ink-4 never carries text a user must read; it numbers, bullets and counts beside text that already reads.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Faces Rule",
        "body": "Figtree speaks only in headings: page titles, the greeting, sheet titles, card titles and the wordmark. Everything a user operates or reads in a row is Geist.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Medium Ceiling Rule",
        "body": "Headings stop at weight 500. 600 is for figures that total something (the Figure, stat values, stage headers and their subtotals, the Total row) and the wordmark.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Money Rule",
        "body": "Every money value, quantity, percentage and document number uses tabular lining figures. Money reads dollars first with the cents at 0.85em in ink-3; turn the grey cents off where the whole figure is already grey, so contrast holds.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Labels, buttons, headers and badges are sentence case. No uppercase labels, no letter-spaced kickers. Headings balance; paragraphs and list items wrap pretty.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline First Rule",
        "body": "Separate with a 1px line (a ring, a hairline or a dashed row rule) before reaching for shadow or tint. Anything heavier than Raised belongs only to an overlay.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the near-black gradient primary for the default action and at most one accent button per screen, only to start a price.",
      "**Do** outline cards with the Card ring and divide rows inside them with dashed rules; keep the Sheet shadow for overlays.",
      "**Do** head a card with a GroupTitle, and build settings and details from Rows and KeyValue lines.",
      "**Do** set every number in tabular figures, money with the cents in ink-3 at 0.85em.",
      "**Do** show status as a grey pill with a word, adding an orange dot only for in flight and a red dot only for failed.",
      "**Do** mark AI-sourced prices with the dashed stamp and keep the tradie's own sources quiet.",
      "**Do** keep targets at least 44px on phones (controls go compact only from 640px) and keep a sheet's primary action at the bottom.",
      "**Do** write labels, buttons and headings in sentence case, with \"Optional\" beside optional fields.",
      "**Do** pluralise and abbreviate units the way the trade writes them, and show a line's markup only when it differs from the default."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use orange for navigation, decoration, selected states or ordinary buttons.",
      "**Don't** use green or red for anything but confirmation and error.",
      "**Don't** set headings above weight 500, set Figtree on controls or rows, or use uppercase or letter-spaced labels and kickers.",
      "**Don't** add icon tiles or per-stage hues (stages are one neutral ramp), and keep gradients to the primary and accent button fills.",
      "**Don't** put text a user must read in ink-4.",
      "**Don't** show errors in modals; use an inline Notice.",
      "**Don't** wrap list tables in a frame; they are open, a grey header over a hairline.",
      "**Don't** introduce radii outside 6 / 7 / 8 / 10 / 14 / 16px and round, or in-page shadows heavier than Raised."
    ]
  }
}